{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.807890Z","id":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","body":{"detail":"Stopping the daemon on exit hangs on AppLifecycleState.detached (runtime close, then supervisor.stop()), which is asynchronous; nothing holds the process open for it. Launching the debug app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME set to a scratch directory and stopping it with SIGTERM left the embedded clax (its PID from <support>/clax-home/daemon.json) running, and it had to be stopped by PID. DaemonSupervisor stops a daemon.json daemon whose /healthz answers with its PID before the next start (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart), so the next launch recovers; until then the daemon holds its port and CLAX_HOME. Whether Cmd-Q delivers detached in time is unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":343},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"2d7228ff0c61c7ee1b84b86a0b4c20e4ba42692f9520c81a978b4e4c6a0a71e8"},"suggested_fix":"On macOS, answer applicationShouldTerminate with terminateLater in AppDelegate.swift, ask Dart over the native channel to stop the worker and the supervisor, then reply to the app.","summary":"A macOS quit or a killed app process can leave the daemon running until the next launch","tags":["needs-verification","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.807991Z","id":"db08c1245a167956dbe7823f1f5bac180303c9bc8395a3ca4d33e4360f9eaecd","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 7 has the WebView reload once a restarted daemon is up, so _AppPage reloads the surface when the endpoint's PID changes. The shell's own event stream reconnects by itself on the same port, so the reload only matters when the page's state went stale; it also discards a composer the person was typing into, and the page's scroll position unless the shell restores it. Reloading only when the shell does not report ready again within a short while would keep the draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":517},"end":{"line":531},"content_hash":"001e3f1ba895d304c889685fc43746a9bb0a245499e84ebeb16f0fbb08b565e5"},"summary":"A daemon restart on the same port reloads the open app, dropping an unsent composer draft","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:23:01.808034Z","id":"e6695aa01ca6e7647778a9d1ebf51e56e2dcec7bee3a22a9a16f506ccc633958","body":{"detail":"AgentRuntime stops the FeedbackWorker on Failed, which cancels the running change through AgentRequest.cancelled; recovery runs it again from the thread once Restart brings the daemon up. A model call that was nearly done is discarded. Keeping the worker running through Failed would let the result publish once the daemon is back, at the cost of polls failing (with backoff up to 10 s) until Restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"c29baf4b0608cc6a7e82f93ce31e00e5cc00ff6782d89986a1a0a9cd96cfb96a"},"summary":"A failed daemon cancels the change in flight, so its model run is paid again after Restart","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T11:59:38.617363Z","id":"add887d20317bdb96b5b99a164e7849b745eef1d91333a14ca15d11c53c5aa6d","body":{"detail":"Failure: quit the macOS app the ordinary way (Cmd-Q, Clax > Quit, or the AppleScript quit event; closing the last window takes the same path through applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed). The app process exits and its clax child keeps running, reparented to launchd, holding its port and CLAX_HOME until the next launch kills it. Reproduced twice against a debug build of f1c07f346b12 (flutter build macos --debug) launched with CFFIXED_USER_HOME set to a scratch directory: osascript -e 'tell application \"<path>/clax_app.app\" to quit' ended the app (PIDs 1346 and 9232) and left clax (1970 and 9246) running with PPID 1; ps after five more seconds still listed it. The relaunch did stop 1970 through daemon.json, so the leak lasts until the next launch. The quit relies on AppLifecycleState.detached, whose handler starts an asynchronous runtime close and supervisor stop that nothing waits for. The osascript reply was error -128 (User canceled): FlutterAppDelegate answers applicationShouldTerminate with a cancel and hands the request to Dart as System.requestAppExit, so the framework's WidgetsBindingObserver.didRequestAppExit hook is called on this path and can hold the quit until the stop finishes.","kind":"blocker","references":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","span":{"start":{"line":343},"end":{"line":352},"content_hash":"2d7228ff0c61c7ee1b84b86a0b4c20e4ba42692f9520c81a978b4e4c6a0a71e8"},"suggested_fix":"Override didRequestAppExit in _AppRootState: await _runtime.close(), then await _s.supervisor.stop() (bounded by its SIGTERM-then-SIGKILL grace), then return AppExitResponse.exit. Test it with tester.binding.handleRequestAppExit() in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart, asserting the supervisor's stopCalls is 1 before the response is exit. Keep the detached path for Android.","summary":"Quitting the macOS app normally leaves the embedded daemon running","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:58.242908Z","id":"a1f75ebee7864e398d194e2c9a309cb3ca6bf2f1df45b3e0c2787273ed4bcf88","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppRoot.didRequestAppExit (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) stops the worker (2 s limit) and then the supervisor (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL; 5 s limit) before answering exit; detach shares the same once-only shutdown, and AppDelegate.applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed already returns true, so closing the last window takes the same path. Test 'quitting the app stops the worker and the daemon first' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart passes (flutter test: +418 ~3 skipped, All other tests passed). Live: flutter build macos --debug, launched the app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME=target/flutter-app/f9-home2 (app PID 35746, daemon PID 36209 from clax-home/daemon.json), ran osascript 'tell application id \"dev.empathic.clax\" to quit': the app exited and kill -0 36209 reported the daemon gone.","supersedes":"d345f33213631fc0427f2bd27b22c1b74778cda22c026ad1e2dfbb6fdeba80b6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:58.243325Z","id":"82f0855007aad4c789bbe5929dd0acec6b77ea215a0384278523063ab20cddc5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"AppRoot.didRequestAppExit (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) stops the worker (2 s limit) and then the supervisor (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL; 5 s limit) before answering exit; detach shares the same once-only shutdown, and AppDelegate.applicationShouldTerminateAfterLastWindowClosed already returns true, so closing the last window takes the same path. Test 'quitting the app stops the worker and the daemon first' in apps/clax_app/test/app_test.dart passes (flutter test: +418 ~3 skipped, All other tests passed). Live: flutter build macos --debug, launched the app with CFFIXED_USER_HOME=target/flutter-app/f9-home2 (app PID 35746, daemon PID 36209 from clax-home/daemon.json), ran osascript 'tell application id \"dev.empathic.clax\" to quit': the app exited and kill -0 36209 reported the daemon gone.","supersedes":"add887d20317bdb96b5b99a164e7849b745eef1d91333a14ca15d11c53c5aa6d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:01.122975Z","id":"a4f13018445ff96dcf721803a039a3bbe9583c77f4b266465aca02c9afa4b624","body":{"detail":"The notification follows MakeStage labels for a make and a fixed 'Working on your comment' for a change. AgentLoop.newApp takes onProgress and the worker emits WorkerProgress (lib/agent/worker.dart:27), but neither is passed to BackgroundRuns.step yet; _onWorker ignores WorkerProgress. Wire a short text from them (for example the size of the page written so far) with _runs.step(run, text).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":485},"content_hash":"e1f97f681e6e08136cf0804ce6d60450068f2a57662275f4abcab8db172f7354"},"summary":"The background notification's progress text is only the making stage; streamed progress is not shown","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.809488Z","id":"308f04f8878c1d07d5d44784b1038f12b1b43c9efd6f8cd129c73c331e39a07f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: lib/app.dart steps the make's and each change's BackgroundRun with progressStep (the latest Narration or ToolStarted label) from newApp's onProgress and from WorkerProgress. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/app_background_test.dart: 'a make shows its narration and tools in the notification, then opens the app', 'a change shows its narration in the notification'. flutter test test/agent test/app_background_test.dart test/app_test.dart test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart: +623, all passed.","supersedes":"a4f13018445ff96dcf721803a039a3bbe9583c77f4b266465aca02c9afa4b624","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.814816Z","id":"1e60b9dd6740e8fa3af86895562b252ab0729fca6883ae81e18e815e7a0c9eb7","body":{"detail":"AgentRuntime stops the FeedbackWorker on Failed, which cancels the running change through AgentRequest.cancelled; recovery runs it again from the thread once Restart brings the daemon up. A model call that was nearly done is discarded. Keeping the worker running through Failed would let the result publish once the daemon is back, at the cost of polls failing (with backoff up to 10 s) until Restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":333},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"e20425a31dc499f287202bd7fac1a475ffd1b2826f73351f3e21f112f08facf3"},"summary":"A failed daemon cancels the change in flight, so its model run is paid again after Restart","supersedes":"e6695aa01ca6e7647778a9d1ebf51e56e2dcec7bee3a22a9a16f506ccc633958","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.815553Z","id":"16065304e8eab625b90a381011139ac6d8cef828f150ec11c0d1f44b6423a497","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 7 has the WebView reload once a restarted daemon is up, so _AppPage reloads the surface when the endpoint's PID changes. The shell's own event stream reconnects by itself on the same port, so the reload only matters when the page's state went stale; it also discards a composer the person was typing into, and the page's scroll position unless the shell restores it. Reloading only when the shell does not report ready again within a short while would keep the draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":937},"end":{"line":952},"content_hash":"fb1d2536c137cd71b52cfbfa3de58ed3c97d8aed3e107879ed4604d777f84c70"},"summary":"A daemon restart on the same port reloads the open app, dropping an unsent composer draft","supersedes":"db08c1245a167956dbe7823f1f5bac180303c9bc8395a3ca4d33e4360f9eaecd","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:56:56.819321Z","id":"7405e1efac450d08971f4c769b7924fcaab0f3508a491d21f05076ad3cbae48b","body":{"detail":"usesToolLoop (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) chooses the tool loop when an inspector is given and the settings' backend takes turns (MessagesApiBackend) or AppServices.runner is set (the debug build's ScriptedRunner from a {\"runs\": …} CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT file). Once U6 passes its WebViewInspector, the worker's and the making screen's runs go through toolLoopRunner (MessagesApiRunner over ResumingTurns on AppServices.clock) with FileAskedQuestions('<support>/asked.json') (already passed by lib/main.dart) and AppServices.readConsent for U6's consent dialog.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"8acffa2fbea63204d0f0c69a86ef326c14e84d1e0314b54002ed36dba2bd9103"},"summary":"For Task U6: the tool loop runs only with AppServices.inspector; lib/main.dart passes none yet, so every run of the running app still takes the single structured call","tags":["handoff","task:U6","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:04.859954Z","id":"a649dc69ccefe6ffbb82d0603682eda2741ce0e9a2d7af8e3738b40ba60792df","body":{"detail":"AppRoot._aimed sends OpenThread once the shell's threads message lists the thread, which selects it in the page (its pin and card). The app screen's own thread page, with the reply and Retry, opens only from the panel (AppScreen._openThread in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart). An AppScreen parameter such as initialThread, opening ThreadDetail after the first ready, would land the person on the reply itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":941},"end":{"line":972},"content_hash":"068865621760b0d52560bb1f7d20da639591d7b4c95d77d451e888a569d0856e"},"summary":"An inbox reply opens its app and asks the shell to select the thread (claxHost.openThread); it does not open the app screen's thread page (ThreadDetail)","tags":["inbox","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:24:30.482928Z","id":"322bd9a4a2e64dd638a8a2f5f7dc5f19e2eab44ce2b84493ec3f6ba29f35d8ea","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: lib/main.dart passes a WebViewInspector (f1c07f346b12) and takes a {\"runs\"} script as the tool loop's runner (f1c07f346b12); AppRoot mounts InspectorHost and builds DialogReadConsent. Evidence: macOS debug build with CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT (str_replace, render, finish) on its real daemon took a sent thread to v2, thread resolved with the agent's reply, GET /api/drafts empty, agent-timings.jsonl {renders: 1, outcome: finished, turns: 3}; finish publishes only after a clean render (lib/agent/tools/finish.dart gate). flutter test: 1199 passed.","supersedes":"7405e1efac450d08971f4c769b7924fcaab0f3508a491d21f05076ad3cbae48b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:07:48.262640Z","id":"84335fdfd947a8ec5bbf90a00fa405959814636972c8cbb81afd0c614f61706a","body":{"detail":"The notice is cleared on the screen leaving the front (app_screen.dart _tellVisible), on quit, and in MainActivity.onDestroy, none of which runs when the process is killed or crashes while the screen is in front. AppRoot's initState does not clear it, so a cold launch from the launcher lands on the home screen with a stale 'Comment on it' notice. Tapping it still routes correctly (launchTap opens that app), so the harm is only a misleading notice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":494},"end":{"line":507},"content_hash":"33bde6b301a55679610acb66f82a16e825cca4a204740251e5d124b8b5229345"},"suggested_fix":"Clear the notice at AppRoot start unless launchTap returned a tap.","summary":"A notice left by a process that died while an app screen was in front stays in the shade after the next launch until an app screen replaces it","tags":["review","u7","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:11:33.677572Z","id":"8bbf34cfdd47d1f2445fd1711a497fc4b23a5e1dd385cd914203e3d33540eb57","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: AppRoot.initState clears AppServices.notice before any app screen shows it. test/app_test.dart \"the notice's actions reach the app on top\" asserts the first call is clear and passes.","supersedes":"84335fdfd947a8ec5bbf90a00fa405959814636972c8cbb81afd0c614f61706a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:25:27.858754Z","id":"454e26ab3f8f097a141e8c9958b5d21f7014e0b60a1a0a21709284c8228c8159","body":{"detail":"AgentLoop.newApp (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:258) keeps the first run's plan under planKey (a fresh 'new:<micros>' when null) and moves it to the app's ID once it is made. AppRoot._make passes none, so nothing can watch PlanStore.watch(key) while the first run plans. The build view (task X1) should make a key starting with pendingPlanPrefix, pass it to newApp, watch it, then watch the app ID.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":800},"end":{"line":806},"content_hash":"8a82c82e08bb71d42bbd1c8d4f11eb3e18c738d86f18186dc31efb31335206d6"},"summary":"The making screen cannot show the plan during a first run: _make does not pass a planKey to AgentLoop.newApp","tags":["handoff","task:X1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:39:53.200044Z","id":"d05d4f17a0d8a8f5d9418138eeb9b44f9133c6e1be58ddd58481bd3474149213","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: AppRoot._make makes a pendingPlanPrefix key when the tool loop runs, reports it as MakePlanKey and passes it to AgentLoop.newApp; MakingScreen watches it, then the app's ID. Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_view_test.dart 'shows the plan from the first run, offers Open app once the first version lands, and follows the build'. flutter test test/ui/build_view_test.dart: +8, all passed; flutter test test/ui test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +419, all passed.","supersedes":"454e26ab3f8f097a141e8c9958b5d21f7014e0b60a1a0a21709284c8228c8159","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:42:41.964543Z","id":"a7ecebe9d62f13cc8d8bc1154baaaa6fcacb2e3f1826f361349eccbe58ce9687","body":{"detail":"_onBuild calls _stepBuild for every BuildState, and the worker emits one per progress event of a continue run. Each call awaits PlanStore.get before BackgroundRuns.step, so two quick events can land in reverse order (an older step overwrites a newer one), and BackgroundRuns.step (platform/background_work.dart:248) dedupes only identical text, so every narration or tool start becomes a notification update. Android drops updates beyond its per-app rate, so the shown step can stick on a stale one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":999},"end":{"line":1020},"content_hash":"c7b762e186894e8ce1ad4a61bbe95ff428cea1471888f3143a582e1acf914f14"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the latest plan from PlanStore.watch per building app instead of a get per event, and throttle notification updates (for example at most one per second, always sending the last).","summary":"The build's notification is updated on every progress event, with a plan read from disk each time, unthrottled and possibly out of order","tags":["review","review:X1","build","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:50:05.964886Z","id":"56c4b64168416cb99b823a1aec91f71646f85ca40c54888c28756d704762f62a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12 and f1c07f346b12: BuildNotices (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/build_notices.dart) shows a build's first state at once, then at most one update each second on the injected clock, the latest state winning, with the plan kept from PlanStore.watch rather than read per event. Test: apps/clax_app/test/ui/build_notices_test.dart. flutter test test/ui test/agent test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +1042, all passed; flutter analyze: no issues.","supersedes":"a7ecebe9d62f13cc8d8bc1154baaaa6fcacb2e3f1826f361349eccbe58ce9687","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:06:24.082502Z","id":"0a2664b07c2795e61f202eed5501b7681ea10c839da055901930003cacd92cc0","body":{"detail":"_failedAway and _offerLostMake push the build view from AppRoot (_makingRoute) and do not read its MakingResult. Edit there cancels the make (MakeSession.cancel) and pops EditRequest, which only the launcher's _showMake (lib/ui/launcher.dart) turns into a New sheet holding the request. Opened from the failed tile instead, Edit works.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":936},"end":{"line":944},"content_hash":"4c89c433a99bbf27aba5b2506d1568a5fc2df439b7856d0ebb1d27fd365ff2f3"},"summary":"A build view opened from the failure toast or from Make it again ignores Edit: the request is dropped instead of reopening the New sheet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:06:24.082564Z","id":"bb075ca4ceab5ecc1ee2d797aee15f3b5591da4e74675963a9dc6f0796b9342b","body":{"detail":"_made holds one app and Timings.start(sayUsable) is started by each make (_make), so a second Make restarts the clock and the first app's ready no longer stops it. The defended number is only right for one make at a time.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":490},"end":{"line":491},"content_hash":"a0e043f9428c26b727c270a80fcf4bb6d712869347b09d2a22becb698a8676c7"},"summary":"say-usable is one slot: with several makes at once it measures from the latest Make to whichever app that run made","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:10:51.019752Z","id":"e0550bb53be343e7d81137215d6b7f905f5bdc49f5a23b9d60028c8389fad7ff","body":{"detail":"_offerLostMake loops over PendingMake.takeAll and awaits a showDialog per request. With three makes cut off, the person answers three modal dialogs before reaching the launcher. One dialog listing the requests (with Make all / pick / Not now) or one making tile per lost request would ask once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":879},"end":{"line":907},"content_hash":"6cc8b9f705848e426ffd0a729d9b98ea98e35bb798047618b06078f0726400b8"},"summary":"Several lost makes at launch ask one 'Make it again?' dialog after another, and 'Not now' on any of them drops that request for good (takeAll deletes the file)","tags":["review","review:X2","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:16.755873Z","id":"66d0645b5949859e2932171aa2bece11b68a381d8608afba78b93d8c691db5ce","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","span":{"start":{"line":879},"end":{"line":907},"content_hash":"c67682eef1911b52161429ae8e4b160c8fc58748e27a465874f7ca373a21d2ad"},"summary":"Fixed: lost makes become Interrupted tiles (MakeService.lost), kept in PendingMake until Make it again or Discard; no launch dialogs. test/app_background_test.dart 'a make the last run never finished is an interrupted tile; Make it again runs it' and 'Discard forgets the lost make; closing the question keeps it' pass.","supersedes":"e0550bb53be343e7d81137215d6b7f905f5bdc49f5a23b9d60028c8389fad7ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:45:00.572970Z","id":"e5416c141b162be686610c1779071206d36ce1f316ed2619205beed44d50a160","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: an inbox reply passes its comment ID (Launcher._openItem, f1c07f346b12) and AppRoot._openTarget hands thread and comment to AppScreen.initialThread/initialComment (f1c07f346b12), which opens ThreadDetail at that comment once the page is first up (f1c07f346b12). Tests pass: test/app_test.dart 'an inbox reply opens its app at the thread once the shell lists it, and its thread page at the reply; a version item at that version', test/ui/app_screen_test.dart 'initialThread opens the thread page at its comment once the page is up', test/ui/thread_detail_test.dart 'a focused comment is scrolled to and lit, then fades'.","supersedes":"a649dc69ccefe6ffbb82d0603682eda2741ce0e9a2d7af8e3738b40ba60792df","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:29.923011Z","id":"bc44acc1e751931a7d1df7f9bafc54e95f1539078763e3dadd8bff8452278de0","body":{"detail":"_presentQuestion adds the ID to _seenQuestions before choosing the background path. Returning to the question's own app still counts it in the change sheet (QuestionsMsg), and the inbox lists it; a launcher or making screen shows nothing until the notification is tapped. A fix: keep background questions in a pending set and present the newest still-open one on AppLifecycleState.resumed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1139},"end":{"line":1173},"content_hash":"ce7bb9deca3d335696cb1236b67af02133ddba62f7271f497b58fe7f93350f4a"},"summary":"A question that arrives while Clax is in the background is only posted as a notification: coming back without tapping it shows no sheet or toast, since the question is marked seen","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:53:29.923190Z","id":"7f28c8ffe91ef10b071c668d3d70c9b37fdf38b4c21bc3d298cceddad56d3ae3","body":{"detail":"The platform side (android/.../BackgroundRunService.kt Notices.news) treats the field as an opaque string extra and keys the notification ID by its hash, so it works without platform changes; but the convention lives only in app.dart. A typed BackgroundWork.question(title, text, qid) with its own tap stream would make it explicit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1122},"end":{"line":1122},"content_hash":"5cc6648706a4d640a900240ac3dfe82f3e35d3e215600e338488790bbbb9590e"},"summary":"A question notification rides on BackgroundWork.ready with the target 'question:<qid>' in its artifact field, which _onNews splits again","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:58:50.476383Z","id":"9757354add87a5bbc24d23b3bc5fa1c067670f0c9445ed1ad0a397161c39aa91","body":{"detail":"Failure: a session asks question A (no app, or with no app screen on top), the sheet opens on A; before A is answered the session (or another) asks B. B gets no sheet, toast or pending slot, and after A closes nothing shows B; it is found only in the inbox, while its asker waits (mode wait, then terminal after terminal_after_s). The same happens when the toast's View or an inbox tap names a question while the sheet shows another. A fix: keep a queue of open questions to present, and on the sheet's whenComplete open the next one still open (or switch the sheet to /inbox, which lists them all).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1175},"end":{"line":1193},"content_hash":"9a1d6b61539acaf98b64b3740aa43eb6a9d511d824118d451a94ac111ad515a3"},"summary":"A second question that lands while the question sheet shows one is dropped: _openQuestion returns on _sheetQuestion != null, and _onQuestionEvent has already marked it seen, so it is never presented","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:58:50.476583Z","id":"2f368b89d08f0eb1dc3ba731c8e6579078a403af1a523f7f396ccdd4fa8371db","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bc44acc1e751931a7d1df7f9bafc54e95f1539078763e3dadd8bff8452278de0","summary":"On macOS this is total: lib/main.dart:155 gives macOS NoBackgroundWork, whose ready() does nothing (lib/platform/background_work.dart:58), so a question that lands while the window is hidden or minimised (AppLifecycleState.hidden, not foreground per lib/platform/network_pause.dart:29-32) posts no notification and is marked seen; coming back shows no sheet or toast. The fix proposed here (present the newest still-open background question on resume) covers both platforms.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:06:03.722222Z","id":"bfe0a98715338b640979d4dfac1cff6d79aea41bda3219b6f3f6acdd458d4c45","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: _showQuestion queues a question while the sheet shows another (or before the daemon is up), and the sheet's whenComplete runs _nextQuestion, skipping questions closed meanwhile. Evidence: test/app_test.dart 'questions asked while the sheet shows one wait for it to close; one answered meanwhile is skipped' (f1c07f346b12); flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: All tests passed (+49).","supersedes":"9757354add87a5bbc24d23b3bc5fa1c067670f0c9445ed1ad0a397161c39aa91","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:06:03.723512Z","id":"d45d5ab96aa8b10aa22c53cdea7c50f84fb9a1a93ed36ee22adb623daaeee116","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: a question posted in the background is kept in _backgroundQuestions and presented through _presentQuestion when AppPresence says foreground again (any platform, so macOS hidden/minimised too): the sheet over Clax's screens, a toast over another app, nothing over its own app; one closed meanwhile is skipped. Evidence: test/app_background_test.dart 'coming back without tapping the notification shows a question still open in the sheet…' and 'a background question about another app is told in a toast on return…' (f1c07f346b12), both failing on the previous app.dart; flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: All tests passed (+49).","supersedes":"bc44acc1e751931a7d1df7f9bafc54e95f1539078763e3dadd8bff8452278de0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:06:03.724675Z","id":"044caf34289a4ef5c49b4884b281f8694755c8cdd407ab2d55478b15f88ccbca","body":{"detail":"_presentQuestion shows a toast with hideCurrentSnackBar for each question not about the app on top, and toasts do not take a sheet slot, so _presentBackgroundQuestions and _nextQuestion present them back to back. The others stay in the inbox and the change sheet's question count. A fix: one toast 'Clax has N questions' whose View opens the first and queues the rest.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1158},"end":{"line":1164},"content_hash":"5bb7ef30fb9a35695f6e3039e5f31b557c8932dd857a696bd32c2dd7c8932eca"},"summary":"Several background questions about other apps, presented on return over an app, each replace the previous toast: only the last one's View shows","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:17.325899Z","id":"e5c1eb520c027cabdf6f014f3bfe0dd9c224f9380787f91d6fac4bc35486bfdc","body":{"detail":"The daemon withdraws hook questions at start (crates/clax-core/src/store/questions.rs:827 withdraw_hook_questions_on_start) before the app's stream resubscribes, and SharedClaxStream reports the gap only as a `resync` event (lib/clax/shared_stream.dart:134), which _onQuestionEvent drops. _questionQueue and _backgroundQuestions survive Failed/Up, and _nextQuestion (scheduled on Up) and _presentBackgroundQuestions trust _openQuestions, so a withdrawn question opens the sheet unprompted. A fix: on a questions resync, refetch the open questions and drop the rest from _openQuestions.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1137},"end":{"line":1154},"content_hash":"341d61e14338a1beaa6ea3ae0d15d5f0ea557c6954c5e47e357105857960844f"},"summary":"_openQuestions ignores the questions topic's resync, so after a daemon restart a queued or background question the daemon withdrew is still presented in the sheet","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:17.326083Z","id":"b5c2b7f2d8ffed40e020ea8b318546d07033e841fee98a6559942333ba62e015","body":{"detail":"On Android the return to the foreground (inactive) reaches didChangeAppLifecycleState before the tap reaches _onNews. With background questions A and B open and B's notification tapped, _presentBackgroundQuestions opens the sheet on A and queues B (asked: false); the tap's _openQuestion(B) upgrades the queued entry to asked and moves it to the end, so the person sees A until they close it. A fix: an asked question goes to the front of the queue, or replaces a sheet opened by _presentBackgroundQuestions.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1209},"end":{"line":1221},"content_hash":"d323815a2b01755ea38bccd4ee8864faca3ce17bbe1dcf84f0d5c395b019fab3"},"summary":"A tapped question notification can show a different question first: coming back presents the oldest background question in the sheet, and the tap's question is queued behind it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:11:52.464807Z","id":"3400659a9be6175bfa618ea306ef4bd7f8a2ca20537668d28043307d80781caf","body":{"detail":"WebViewAppSurface sets the key cookie before each load and reload (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart _setKey). WebViewQuestionPage (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/question_sheet.dart) has no such hook: it relies on the cookie this listener puts in the shared WebView cookie store on each Up, which is asynchronous, so a load that starts before setCookie completes is answered 401. After a daemon restart (new token, same port) an open shell's token, owner and events cookies are stale: its requests are 401 until the shell asks /api/token again with the new key cookie, or the page reloads. Checked on macOS for WebViewAppSurface only (apps/clax_app/integration_test/locked_daemon_test.dart); the question page and Android are unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"3bf62e9b3cfc04c844c500d4d6474bf874c0244672c552c6fc7e71ec6aba392b"},"summary":"WebViews other than WebViewAppSurface get the key cookie only from the Up listener, and an open shell is not reloaded after a restart","tags":["security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:12:27.615216Z","id":"66663ece3e306bea67d919ccb0e36499641bf13fdce664ad21cc8b65a19cb923","body":{"detail":"Failure: any new app made on the tool loop (an inspector, a Messages API or scripted runner) whose making screen hands over with a last render (_handOver passes lastFrame as the cover). _AppPageState.build returns Stack([screen, made-cover]) while _cover is set and the bare screen once the shell's Ready uncovers it; the screen changes parent, so its AppScreen element is unmounted and mounted again: the first AppScreenState's dispose calls widget.surface.dispose(), and the new one starts with _covered = true and never sees a Ready (the shell already sent it). Seen in apps/clax_app/integration_test/tool_loop_test.dart (macOS, real daemon and WebViewInspector): the rig's listener got Ready for v1, 'made-cover' was gone and 'app-cover' (the spinner) stayed, so the two-finger swipe never reached the page (log target/flutter-app/i1-tool.log). The single-call path (full_loop_test.dart) hands over without a cover and does not hit it. test/app_background_test.dart checks only that 'made-cover' goes, not that the page is uncovered.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1601},"end":{"line":1624},"content_hash":"16dba17a1439da31f2468506b078b480b62f83420c1edfacc523a3e11e547295"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the tree shape fixed: always return Stack(fit: StackFit.expand, children: [screen, if (cover != null) ColoredBox(...)]) (or give the screen a GlobalKey), and in app_background_test.dart's hand-over test expect find.byKey(ValueKey('app-cover')) to find nothing after the Ready.","summary":"A tool-loop make handed over with its last render as the cover leaves the app screen covered by its spinner for good","tags":["review","integration","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:50.990979Z","id":"cac571968f7b4145833b157c87bc20a45ee9c85e6ca8726580b03ca0e4be4ca9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: _AppPage builds the same Stack with or without the made-cover, so the Ready that removes it keeps the AppScreen. test/app_background_test.dart 'a make streams to the making screen, which hands over to the new app in its place, covered by the last render until ready' now checks the same AppScreen State survives, its surface is not disposed and no app-cover remains; it failed before the fix (line 769) and passes (flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +54, all passed).","supersedes":"66663ece3e306bea67d919ccb0e36499641bf13fdce664ad21cc8b65a19cb923","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:51.020832Z","id":"5661277371f76c7c0c1266b08fab426dd1e7af8a9f23d61239ecfc98adfe7e01","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: a questions resync, Up with a queue and the return to the foreground recheck open questions with ClaxApi.questions (_recheckQuestions) and drop the ones no longer open. Tests (failed before f1c07f346b12, pass after; flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +54, all passed): app_test.dart 'a queued question the daemon withdrew without a stream event is dropped on the questions resync', 'after a daemon restart a queued question it withdrew is not shown'; app_background_test.dart 'a background question the daemon withdrew without a stream event is not shown on return'.","supersedes":"e5c1eb520c027cabdf6f014f3bfe0dd9c224f9380787f91d6fac4bc35486bfdc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:51.050415Z","id":"ecc3d14d6c97969107f5120ec7b88d9709944188b7053d706c013b449fe5600b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: an asked question queues ahead of new ones and takes the place of a sheet showing an unasked one, which goes back to the queue behind it; background presentation also waits for the recheck. app_background_test.dart 'a tapped question notification shows its question first, the other background question after it' failed before (showed A) and passes (flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +54, all passed).","supersedes":"b5c2b7f2d8ffed40e020ea8b318546d07033e841fee98a6559942333ba62e015","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:19:51.080438Z","id":"6a7d84f46e3b5fd71c8f5af18d3e5333556c2739952ad91a0e13d11f3c782b6d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: _presentQuestions tells all questions about other apps over an app in one toast ('Clax has N questions' when several), whose View opens each in turn; _nextQuestion gathers them too. app_background_test.dart 'several background questions about other apps are told in one toast on return; its View shows each in turn' failed before and passes (flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +54, all passed).","supersedes":"044caf34289a4ef5c49b4884b281f8694755c8cdd407ab2d55478b15f88ccbca","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:22:33.326750Z","id":"ff4575c41b4112330d0cea4454a26e151fc9fe7ab091aa0c8d92eaf9d0f0f915","body":{"detail":"The removal loop runs over _openQuestions as it is when the response lands, not as it was when the request went out. A question event handled during the await (e.g. one asked just after a questions resync, or just after the daemon comes up in _recheckThenNext) is absent from the older snapshot, so it is removed from _openQuestions and _backgroundQuestions and added to _seenQuestions. If it was queued behind a showing sheet, _nextQuestion (app.dart:1366-1367) then skips it; a tapped notification for it is skipped too (seen, no view). The inbox still lists it. A live close cannot be undone by the recheck (it only removes), so answers are safe.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1174},"end":{"line":1188},"content_hash":"00e55b5d8d8858fa6dcd646ade1b41e7358186faaa6f175d71f453a326b537e2"},"suggested_fix":"Snapshot [..._openQuestions.keys] before the await and only drop IDs from that snapshot that the response lacks.","summary":"_recheckQuestions drops a question that arrives on the stream while its questions() request is in flight, so a queued or background question can be lost","tags":["review","N2c","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:22:33.326902Z","id":"cd7c2dac4b3dd02b0513fb7a6a30c0adf260f63ef4ac12c9945594f3ececdd5b","body":{"detail":"test/app_background_test.dart's tapped-notification test opens the asked question before the recheck queues the other, so the sheet it replaces is never showing; no test in test/app_test.dart or test/app_background_test.dart reaches removeRoute. By reading, the path is sound on the installed SDK: NavigatorState.removeRoute completes the route's future (navigator.dart:5733-5751, entry.complete), so whenComplete clears _sheetQuestion/_sheetRoute and shows the asked one, and a second asked question in the same window is queued without a second removeRoute (route.isActive is false). A regression here would leave a stuck _sheetQuestion and no further sheets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1302},"end":{"line":1315},"content_hash":"428f44233f73c4f3db86016370b266794031ce5532b86d32d5efbee76bb90ede"},"suggested_fix":"A test in test/app_test.dart: a question about no app shows its sheet unasked, then the inbox opens a second; expect the second loaded, and after Close the first again.","summary":"The path where an asked question takes the place of an unasked sheet (removeRoute, then the old completion shows the asked one) has no test","tags":["review","N2c","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:24:37.100739Z","id":"e95192ea8e1b80cd9cebb8fbafff38b1977b3a7afe791a0f09ac4685a03f18ef","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: _recheckQuestions copies the open question keys before the await and drops only those. f1c07f346b12 adds 'a question that lands while the recheck is in flight is kept' (FakeClaxApi.holdQuestions holds the answer while a second question lands); it failed before the fix (QuestionWebSheet not found after closing the first) and passes now. flutter test test/app_test.dart test/app_background_test.dart: +55, All tests passed.","supersedes":"ff4575c41b4112330d0cea4454a26e151fc9fe7ab091aa0c8d92eaf9d0f0f915","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:30:27.959670Z","id":"3dcd3b96b028e2005d4524de864f7cfb72aedd7ccc668c370fba002b6f9df083","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Every daemon WebView loads through CookieLoads (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/daemon_cookie.dart), which awaits DaemonKeyCookie.ready before each load and reload: WebViewAppSurface (shell and inspector) and WebViewQuestionPage, which main.dart now passes to AppServices.questionPage. On a restart, main.dart's Up listener calls DaemonKeyCookie.refresh; a new token's cookie is set first, then restarts fires and a loaded question page reloads (followRestarts). An open app page already reloads on the endpoint's new PID (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart _AppPageState._onEndpoint), through the same awaited cookie. flutter test test/ui/daemon_cookie_test.dart: 6 passed (load and reload wait for a cookie write held open by the test; a loaded page following restarts reloads after the new cookie is set; an unloaded or disposed page does not). A real WebView run on Android stays open on 18cb7cff.","supersedes":"3400659a9be6175bfa618ea306ef4bd7f8a2ca20537668d28043307d80781caf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:17:45.428307Z","id":"c8e36cbdd1773918755742af1ce5885ee80428176554a939988c804eef387a7d","body":{"detail":"test/app_bundles_test.dart covers a file opened before the daemon is up, a refusal and forgetDeleted. Nothing tests that _recoverBundles shows one BundleNoticeSheet per RecoveredUpdate and the 'Shared apps' damaged notice exactly once (only _bundlesStarted guards them), that two files opened together show their sheets one after another through _bundleQueue, or that delete is false off Android (line 796): flutter test runs as android, so the macOS branch that must never delete the person's own file has no test. A sheet dropped because _nav.currentContext is null (line 763) also leaves Android's cache copy undeleted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":774},"end":{"line":845},"content_hash":"60cf79913f56f65c23568a53ee22cff2c487e1a3f5e808694c402dce092e8b35"},"suggested_fix":"App tests with debugDefaultTargetPlatformOverride = TargetPlatform.macOS asserting the opened file still exists; a pre-written snapshot under supportDir/snapshots and an unreadable lineage file, asserting each notice once across a daemon restart; two FakeBundleIntake.open calls in a row.","summary":"The start-up bundle wiring's notices and platform rule are untested: recoverInterrupted's notices, the damaged-lineage notice, several queued files, and macOS keeping the opened file","tags":["bundles","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:25:17.928336Z","id":"6833bf1756e0ebca997dc05c4de5f78f1d527e5a1b75694e14d7abc72938c3fb","body":{"detail":"HomeHost.summaries leaves out only settings.homeAppId (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_host.dart). Installer.install (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart) creates the artifact, writes its lineage entry, seeds documents and keeps the bundle before it returns the ID, and the Launcher behind HomeRoute redraws on the gallery event in between. Seen only in the fallback grid, until the home app's first ready replaces it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":881},"end":{"line":898},"content_hash":"c93628b91fdcdb1e4dadae78f1d415ea78f45fad9e5b684b13215cd12e9cd4b2"},"summary":"On the first run the built-in home screen can list the home app's own tile ('Home') for a moment: the installer's createArtifact fires a gallery version event before ensureHomeApp saves homeAppId and settingsChanged hides it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:33:46.083901Z","id":"ca3db4aea35a882c0a0cf30af3fd5d5c59288a1750615da0432cc5c918eeea3b","body":{"detail":"Failure: first run (no home.json) or any start where the home app is installed while the built-in screen shows: HomeRoute (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_route.dart, cover = ... _fellBack && _ready != load) lifts the built-in Launcher at the page's first Ready, which the shell posts on each frame load (Ready in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart:105-124). At that moment the home app's Home component (apps/clax_app/home/home.js:482-505) still has apps === null, because use('home') and apps() are two device round trips after load, so it renders body = null: the Launcher's tiles go and an empty page with only the bar and New app shows until apps() answers. The route test 'a home app installed while the built-in screen shows takes over...' (apps/clax_app/test/home/home_route_test.dart:131) fakes ready only, so it cannot see this. The 10 s no-ready rule planned for the fallback uses the same signal.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1891},"end":{"line":1907},"content_hash":"4dd809d3176e301ac198f17405116998ba45add6b40ed84eebfb016c0a5e6450"},"suggested_fix":"Lift the cover on a signal the page gives once its grid is drawn: e.g. the first home apps() call answered to the home app followed by a page-side call (home.shown(), or the kit's claude.ready()) made after the first render with apps; keep frame-load ready only as the 'page alive' signal for the 10 s rule. Test with a fake surface whose ready precedes its apps() call.","summary":"The first-run swap from the built-in home screen to the home app happens at the shell's frame-load ready, before the home app has its apps: the person sees the bar and New app button over an empty grid","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:33:46.084072Z","id":"f612a838a9f94615940ec0549bbbd1a6cb1a47a820f2681dc621c4baa07f998a","body":{"detail":"_installHome runs once, from _startBundles (guarded by _bundlesStarted, app.dart:850-859). Any exception from ensureHomeApp is printed and dropped, so a daemon Restarting -> Up during the first run leaves the built-in home screen for the whole session. Likewise a recorded home app deleted while Clax runs (web gallery, agent) leaves HomeRoute showing an AppScreen for a missing artifact until restart: nothing listens for artifact_deleted of settings.homeAppId.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":884},"end":{"line":900},"content_hash":"ccc8444b9156641433c94dd6f2ffa6bd07b13667641b58190867da37855c73c5"},"suggested_fix":"Run _installHome on each Up until it succeeds once, and on HomeHost seeing artifact_deleted for homeAppId clear it and install again (or fall back).","summary":"A home app install that fails (daemon restarting, a blip on getArtifact) is not tried again until the app is next launched","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:33:46.084158Z","id":"07af4dec4b3025e77e4e5a22d61f9430e464a07aab60f4b6f48dcd11d6214a35","body":{"detail":"While HomeRoute keeps the Launcher over the home app (first-run load, and the failed state the fallback banner adds), the AppScreen below is in the same route and resumed, so _tellVisible (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart, _lifecycleShown && _routeCurrent) tells it visible: initState registers its toggles on the shared CommentsCommand (macOS Comment/Threads act on the hidden page), its Focus(autofocus: true) and Escape binding sit under the Launcher, its PopScope takes system back first when its page has history, and home events go to it rather than being held for catch-up.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1891},"end":{"line":1907},"content_hash":"4dd809d3176e301ac198f17405116998ba45add6b40ed84eebfb016c0a5e6450"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the cover state into the home AppScreen (e.g. a covered flag or a TickerMode/Offstage-style wrapper HomeRoute sets), and count it in _tellVisible like a covering route.","summary":"The home app's screen under the built-in screen's cover counts itself shown: it holds the menu bar's Comment and Threads, autofocus and back","tags":["review","home","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:33:46.084227Z","id":"cea3964d1be5a9a92d0d968231bf8c129f5d0cd0f5c4a70647fff12685ac2166","body":{"detail":"In the app, both the home app and the built-in Launcher act through _homeFlows with contextOf: () => _nav.currentContext (the Navigator's own element). apps/clax_app/test/ui/launcher_test.dart builds Launcher without host, so its flows use the Launcher's context; apps/clax_app/test/home/home_route_test.dart checks the menu rect reaching HomeActions but not the flows. A context lookup that needs something below the Navigator (Overlay.of, Scaffold.of, a render box for a share origin in BundleFlows) would fail only in the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":615},"end":{"line":633},"content_hash":"2daa441da94fc6f424a485ab97be19e5b691ee70483a25ead316d6945e4115d0"},"suggested_fix":"Add an AppRoot-level widget test: a home device call openInbox/menu/newApp from the home AppScreen shows the inbox route, the menu sheet and the New app sheet, and the built-in Launcher with host: does the same.","summary":"No test drives HomeFlows over the app navigator's context: the home app's inbox, menu sheet, import and New app flows are tested only through a Launcher that builds its own HomeFlows","tags":["review","home","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T15:35:57.495602Z","id":"4bab0857e48d0cbf80d12c9a12528cb65f7590d43225054745a679e9b96ed55a","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/test/home/home_update_test.dart covers updateHomeApp over the real Updater and a FakeInspector; the wiring in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart that builds the Installer, passes updater.update and completes the sheet's Completer from _bundleQueue is exercised only on a device.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":884},"end":{"line":924},"content_hash":"2f0f90a7721a234c655330d4b3d93742bd179a22fd3e3ddc3fa5816e3153d443"},"summary":"The startup home update (updateHomeApp in _installHome) has no app-level test: no test passes shippedHome to AppRoot, so the ask callback over _bundleSheet, its null answer when no screen is up, and a null _updater (no inspector) are untested","tags":["home-app","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:33.597354Z","id":"dcdf2645188638b85087674ca3a63ec5483fa20d11cc89cae3567c58ff514fa6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: HomeRoute lifts the built-in cover on the page's home.shown() (home.js calls it after the first render with apps), not on the frame's ready; no shown within 10 s falls back. Evidence: flutter test test/home/home_route_test.dart (the install test pushes Ready, then available/apps device calls, then shown; the cover stays until shown) passes, 16 tests; npx playwright test e2e/home-app.spec.ts passes, 8 tests, asserting shown follows apps once.","supersedes":"ca3db4aea35a882c0a0cf30af3fd5d5c59288a1750615da0432cc5c918eeea3b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:33.652144Z","id":"08460aba3a246e74ce9442b0d536fdf289e7d07c3c1c12a1b7221cdefb31af07","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: HomeKeeper (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_keeper.dart) retries ensureHomeApp with a doubling wait (1 s to 60 s), at each daemon Up, and on artifact_deleted of homeAppId after showing the built-in screen. Evidence: flutter test test/home/home_keeper_test.dart passes, 5 tests.","supersedes":"f612a838a9f94615940ec0549bbbd1a6cb1a47a820f2681dc621c4baa07f998a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:05:33.706473Z","id":"0e8c72b326c3f9030c3c33fa3ea3fb434754814f1215d6a5e8e9ac5507690650","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: AppScreen.covered (from HomeRoute's HomePageHooks.covered) counts the screen hidden: no CommentsCommand registration, ExcludeFocus, back not taken, home events held for catch-up. Evidence: flutter test test/home/home_route_test.dart 'the home app under the built-in screen acts as covered' passes.","supersedes":"07af4dec4b3025e77e4e5a22d61f9430e464a07aab60f4b6f48dcd11d6214a35","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:45:28.697502Z","id":"21417a8a8d4ccfaed3198e447cbccbd70efccbab9c06cc73a995dcbe798eac4c","body":{"detail":"The home app's WebView is made by the home route at the daemon's first Up, so its process start, the shell's load and the page's first render follow the daemon's start. On the macOS release build main to the home app's first shown took 358-632 ms over five cold starts (f1c07f346b12), small enough that a WebView made before Up, handed its base URL later, was not worth a new AppSurface factory.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2069},"end":{"line":2087},"content_hash":"f687d212a4ef2f2498ef56a6024ff9f5185a0ef49a8da61de7b66e6640541d6a"},"summary":"Start the home app's WebView (WebKit's or Chromium's process) before the daemon is up, and load the shell once it is","tags":["time-to-usable","revisit:home-usable on the phone is over the target set from its first measurement","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:49:53.490385Z","id":"51fed27a8931c887d8ca7aa1155308817ad9ec637444041e6c5d9f344aba2814","body":{"detail":"main.dart starts homeUsable at launch; _watchHome stops it at the first HomeHost.shown of the session. With 'Use the built-in home screen' on, the 10 s rule firing, or the install failing, no shown comes at launch, so the interval stays open and is stopped later by the first shown after Undo, Reset or turning the built-in screen off, recording minutes or hours as launch-to-usable. The Settings timings list and any gate set from the first measurement then read those values. Options: drop the start (a Timings cancel) when HomeRoute first settles on the built-in screen or HomeSnapshotCover.drop runs, or record only a shown that lands within shownWithin of launch. The extra 'snapshot': _homeCover != null also says true when the cover was dropped.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2030},"end":{"line":2037},"content_hash":"21a3518d678eb2927f816486ee3bc1e5d57deafcc0bca3ea01a4b1a3da502034"},"summary":"home-usable keeps running when the launch's home screen is the built-in one, and records whatever time passes until the home app's next shown","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T17:59:17.298326Z","id":"80da68a3d4cfb2093563a1d2932c2246ac34af3d51a524c5db22f0b5f933d12e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12: AppRoot ends home-usable only while _launchOpen, which HomeRoute.onBuiltIn (the built-in screen shown) and a daemon failure clear; the 'snapshot' extra reads whether the cover still showed. flutter test test/home/app_home_test.dart -> passes 'a launch that shows the built-in home screen records no home-usable, not even at a later shown', which fails with the _launchOpen check removed.","supersedes":"51fed27a8931c887d8ca7aa1155308817ad9ec637444041e6c5d9f344aba2814","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:09:26.692785Z","id":"a2be967cade9354cbb187a96566e24aae8a336f2ca16f068e1d9f8be12e18e11","body":{"detail":"_onEndpoint reloads the page only when the endpoint's pid or base changes. With DaemonHost.inProcess (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/in_process.dart) every run's RunningProcess.pid is the app's own PID, and the supervisor asks for the kept port (<support>/daemon-port), so after onResume restarts a daemon whose listener iOS reclaimed, the new endpoint has the same pid and base and only a new token. The page is not reloaded on the new daemon; its live stream reconnects only if the shell does it on its own. Test that would catch it: an _AppPage given an endpoint with the same pid and base and a new token reloads its surface.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2410},"end":{"line":2424},"content_hash":"adac3c47bcf8c359ff84bf34d325c3c8bbb525ce71ae9026efc3cece0411d5e4"},"suggested_fix":"Compare the endpoint's token as well (e.pid == _pid && e.base == _base && e.token == _token), or carry a run counter in DaemonEndpoint.","summary":"An open app page does not reload when an in-process daemon restarts: its endpoint keeps the same PID and base","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:14:46.536996Z","id":"c42ff35b4bbbf23e9d14576bd86690421ab97e3441fdbf2f99da8ef405b8d816","body":{"detail":"ClaxPointerScope (lib/ui/kit/verbs.dart) records the kind from a translucent Listener at the root. Widget tests drive Flutter-drawn surfaces only. On Android the platform view's touches pass through Flutter's hit testing, so this likely holds there; on macOS it falls back to Click by platform before any event either way. The home app's chrome().pointer and the notifications' Tap/Click follow the same value.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2347},"end":{"line":2347},"content_hash":"ea118f4fd4593c995968e58cde5b18ee551960264645958f19ea01ce61eab3d4"},"suggested_fix":"Check on a Chromebook or Android with a mouse: move the mouse over the home app's page only, then trigger a no_gesture notice and read Tap or Click.","summary":"Whether pointer events over an app's WebView (a platform view) reach ClaxPointerScope's Listener is not verified on a device; if they do not, a Chromebook mouse used only in a page keeps saying Tap","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:02.421312Z","id":"91e1215371bd93210cf13abca64345d4a45019a65f27f855d45c6eb7301234ba","body":{"detail":"The tool loop's runner is _s.runner?.call() ?? toolLoopRunner(...); only toolLoopRunner wraps the backend in ResumingTurns, which is where a pause aborts and holds a turn. A scripted build (CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT) therefore runs on while paused, and a simulator test that pauses one through expireBackgroundTask sees the notice and pauseDone but no held run. Test that would catch it: an app test with a ScriptedRunner whose run is in flight when stopped arrives with pausesRuns, expecting it held until resumed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1180},"end":{"line":1182},"content_hash":"e8ee1480d97781bf828ed480a953542ba42fbf1c42544c493b74e8493a1bd381"},"summary":"A run on the AppServices.runner override (the debug build's ScriptedRunner) is not paused by AppPresence.pause: it never goes through ResumingTurns","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:02.422035Z","id":"e4ce7b4ca881262e618fdba91326c48864112483697eb2ff7e217a669e04fca0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: _AppPageState._onEndpoint compares the token too; test 'an in-process daemon restarted on the same port and PID, with a new token, reloads the open app' passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:app_test), and fails with the token comparison taken out.","supersedes":"a2be967cade9354cbb187a96566e24aae8a336f2ca16f068e1d9f8be12e18e11","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:09:47.739034Z","id":"84075eea14fc7f7497cd46e6a0653d1b6f0dd533874cf4d61a8d5b3489e2fcef","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: home_host_test 'an app a home install makes is never listed, even before homeAppId is saved' passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:home_home_host_test); without installing: it fails listing the new app. HomeHost.installing hides the app from Installer.install's made callback on, and holds list answers and gallery fetches until the daemon made it.","supersedes":"6833bf1756e0ebca997dc05c4de5f78f1d527e5a1b75694e14d7abc72938c3fb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:26:16.972310Z","id":"b5f3e84d8362eeb2e36c541137c54b0e568db1faa9f8e581236e33e6090ec6c5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: AppRoot sets a ScriptedRunner's hold to wait out a pause (AppPresence.paused, until whenForeground), and ScriptedRunner waits on it before each call. //apps/clax_app:integration_ios_pause passes 3 of 3 runs (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_ios_pause --runs_per_test=3): the scripted make is held at its first step after expireBackgroundTask and finishes once Clax is back; with the hold line removed from lib/app.dart the same test fails with 'timed out waiting for the run held at its first step'. //apps/clax_app:agent_runner_scripted_runner_test passes.","supersedes":"91e1215371bd93210cf13abca64345d4a45019a65f27f855d45c6eb7301234ba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:55:47.353653Z","id":"f749c22d8f0f376be905aa8188ca087c807146338a2fa3ae18600710a3b7a7a5","body":{"detail":"_mayRun answers false when _nav has no mounted context, and _gateRun then calls FeedbackWorker.cancelChange or stopBuild, so the comments stay stopped until a newer comment or Retry. Unlike DialogReadConsent (waiting: _runs.needsOk), the sheet posts no notification when Clax is in the background, so a change recovered at a launch that ends before the first frame would be stopped silently. Only the loop's gate is tested (test/agent/ai_consent_test.dart); no app-level test drives a change through _gateRun.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":757},"end":{"line":775},"content_hash":"cbe4b2b81135a791b6f28c0cd7ee999e9e987dcb9be59fe148b67bcf241a5e33"},"summary":"A change or build the AI consent stops while no navigator is up is stopped as Stop stops it, with nothing told in the background","tags":["ios","untested","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T14:37:28.651849Z","id":"83ac0c7bbb8659b8e6f6798fdf9f45654b647988b0eac46ca6541285e5ae3ef9","body":{"detail":"PendingMake keeps only requests, so a stopped MakeSession does not come back after a quit; _offerLostMake then removes every 'new:' entry of unfinished.json. Up to $6 of drafted work is lost if Clax quits before Keep going. Keeping it would mean saving the stopped make's key with its request in PendingMake and offering it as a stopped tile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1646},"end":{"line":1660},"content_hash":"66ed153bd77c2b62fbd32bfc6448afe90f34af15e4db187538806cd496e1fdec"},"summary":"A make stopped at a limit is not kept across launches: its draft is forgotten at the next launch","tags":["make","keep-going","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230722Z","id":"4050e41739e610b48071a5d4e89041c50a3b71ebe19a818fe9ef1b87cc9667ea","body":{"detail":"_open selects the app in the sidebar only for a plain open; the inbox's thread links, a version, a draft comment and a notice's Comment or Threads push _appRoute over the split as before. The detail's _AppPage is not in _openApps, so _openFromNotice and _openRoute do not see it as the top app (a notice for it pushes a second screen of it), and its actions stream is empty.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2232},"end":{"line":2248},"content_hash":"5446dcd444025cc501cfca32f720ece8cccf4fbf06cf1d52b29a325c7ad23ec0"},"suggested_fix":"Keep an _OpenApp for the split detail (without a route) and aim it (thread, version, comment, action) in place, as the pushed route's surface is aimed.","summary":"In a split window an app opened at a thread, a version or a comment, or with an action, is still pushed over the whole window, and the app in the detail is not one of _openApps","tags":["split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230805Z","id":"c0224910d6a355920bb21cbc622bcbfa52d7d9c6f76535bb4b459975f6e0af82","body":{"detail":"Spec §4.9 and §5.6 (plan Task 51) put the making view in the detail pane; until then _MakeDetail in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart is a placeholder that opens HomeActions.openMake.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2626},"end":{"line":2629},"content_hash":"9dd08694699ac14f2f0ae61fed649d390f46840cf5e27025002c7fd9fa1d89f2"},"summary":"A make selected in the sidebar shows only its request, state and Show progress, which pushes the build view","tags":["split","revisit:the making view sits in the detail pane","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230879Z","id":"ef5e2ac6e0936a00acbf5c8a18401dab8b9d274cd3bd08044cb2107ce899c8cb","body":{"detail":"Spec §5.11's Mac case opens the window with the sidebar drawn from HomeHost's cached lists and the working ClaxMark in the detail after 600 ms. _home returns ClaxSplash (or the launch snapshot) until the daemon's first Up creates HomeHost, and SidebarModel needs a HomeHost; nothing caches the lists across launches.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2578},"end":{"line":2582},"content_hash":"860feff50060936360dda048cb4b81efdc861d086d0e030a29cec554b652ffb0"},"summary":"The split window shows only once HomeHost exists: before the daemon is up the splash fills the window","tags":["macos","split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:48:37.753940Z","id":"1fe84658f010d0eb1d96d1f21a32972a2ad10c439859398e5e118141e7143ce0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: a make in a split window shows its build view (MakingScreen with onExit) in the detail. test/app_test.dart 'a wide Mac window makes a new app in its detail: …' passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:app_test).","supersedes":"c0224910d6a355920bb21cbc622bcbfa52d7d9c6f76535bb4b459975f6e0af82","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:48:38.694445Z","id":"07a96334a06a948badec5fbb7caa67a3417a3912686d0b719f5ef26623f779b0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0a2664b07c2795e61f202eed5501b7681ea10c839da055901930003cacd92cc0","summary":"Commit f1c07f346b12 routes _stoppedAway and _failedAway through HomeFlows.showMake (lib/app.dart _showMaking), whose result goes to HomeFlows.makingLeft (lib/ui/launcher.dart:1220), which turns EditRequest into the New sheet holding the request; _makingRoute is pushed only before HomeHost exists. No test drives Edit from a toast-opened build view, so this is left open for a test or the owner's close.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:48:38.694682Z","id":"399cb81f8b4588605d9a72403d7f6ab0d486c1a4df40401c63daa601af07a86c","body":{"detail":"MakingScreen in the detail draws its leading (build-back, a chevron) through ClaxScaffold's Mac header in the toolbar row of the detail (WindowTitlebar.of), where macos/Runner/Toolbar.swift puts Back and Forward past the sidebar's edge. test/ui/shots/split_shots_test.dart draws the toolbar's items as stand-ins over it, so the render (split-make-mac-*.png) cannot show an overlap. The WKWebView preview at the pane's width (up to 960) is also seen only through a fake PreviewView.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2762},"end":{"line":2800},"content_hash":"4065c8f7d7eb77768568edf560df001acd0079f450fbe2af996adf20e897f0b4"},"summary":"The build view in a split window's detail is unverified in the running Mac app, and its Back header shares the toolbar row with the native Back and Forward","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:48:38.694795Z","id":"191a38cc31b740c096bf4df079981bcb6fec43a4abab9a348de51b80b740e3e9","body":{"detail":"MakeService removes a made session from its list, so the make's row goes; SidebarModel.keeps (lib/ui/split/sidebar_model.dart:281) keeps MakeSelected while _paneMake names it, so MakingScreen can follow the build until Open app. No app test drives a make with a plan that goes on (the app_test rig hands the app over at once), and the window's title stays the request. _paneMake is cleared only when the view exits, not when the person selects something else.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2762},"end":{"line":2800},"content_hash":"4065c8f7d7eb77768568edf560df001acd0079f450fbe2af996adf20e897f0b4"},"summary":"A made make whose build goes on keeps its build view selected in the detail with no sidebar row selected; the path has no test","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.976753Z","id":"4cf28bd1985c375b3491c9538a74cbf2eb954921f3231a834523d1c90107a4a7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"399cb81f8b4588605d9a72403d7f6ab0d486c1a4df40401c63daa601af07a86c","summary":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f1c07f346b12 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): with a make selected the window's toolbar declares no items, so the build view's Back (225–265 points from the left, in the toolbar row) shares the row with no native Back or Forward (make-light/dark.png). The WKWebView preview at the pane's width was not seen: the held make never wrote a page.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:06:48.514146Z","id":"be84a65ee946bbe9efb8aa7a12ee1b4c52af5b111328c37272dccda6abfc8942","body":{"detail":"Launcher builds its own HomeFlows (lib/ui/launcher.dart) with no showInbox, and reads no chrome(), so the rail's hold of the toolbar (SplitShellState._report) does not reach it. Only the home app's flows (AppRootState._homeFlows, showInbox: _showInbox) open the rail's Inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2847},"end":{"line":2848},"content_hash":"6dc1d18f99c052558559d5250e6a0635adfd7ee555b97b3ae4a1954f48d315c6"},"summary":"The built-in launcher (the fallback home screen) in a wide Android split still draws its own bar beside the rail, and its Inbox button pushes InboxScreen as a route through its own HomeFlows instead of the rail's Inbox destination","tags":["android","split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:36:00.076098Z","id":"aadbfeaf5ead4dcc3b3c7d4ea0a22eee0167b42617a4ef459e49a4ecc2ccc746","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4050e41739e610b48071a5d4e89041c50a3b71ebe19a818fe9ef1b87cc9667ea","summary":"Since f1c07f346b12 the rail's Inbox shows a reply's thread inside the inbox (beside the list from expanded, in the list's place at medium) instead of pushing it. Still pushed over the whole window: the thread page's Open app, a version's Open app and a version preview from the thread (InboxSplit._openApp and onPreview in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inbox/inbox_split.dart call AppRootState._openTarget with a thread or version, which _open pushes as _appRoute).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T22:36:00.142662Z","id":"8dc86773b52f8251f416db0346de6722b2e27c6a80e6d921a6ab260668f88828","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: 'while a split window holds the toolbar, the launcher draws no bar and no New app of its own' (test/ui/launcher_test.dart) and 'beside a wide Android rail the built-in home screen leaves New app, Inbox and Settings to the rail; at 700 its own Inbox opens the rail's' (test/app_test.dart) pass (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:ui_launcher_test //apps/clax_app:app_test). The launcher's Inbox already went through the host's HomeFlows (AppRootState._homeFlows.showInbox), opening the rail's Inbox.","supersedes":"be84a65ee946bbe9efb8aa7a12ee1b4c52af5b111328c37272dccda6abfc8942","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:12.694889Z","id":"095988b7d19775e2f4c70d894be2d895bf7dead7f9f101a1b9a47cd7387b9be0","body":{"detail":"AgentRuntime stops the FeedbackWorker on Failed, which cancels the running change through AgentRequest.cancelled; recovery runs it again from the thread once Restart brings the daemon up. A model call that was nearly done is discarded. Keeping the worker running through Failed would let the result publish once the daemon is back, at the cost of polls failing (with backoff up to 10 s) until Restart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":496},"end":{"line":505},"content_hash":"e20425a31dc499f287202bd7fac1a475ffd1b2826f73351f3e21f112f08facf3"},"summary":"A failed daemon cancels the change in flight, so its model run is paid again after Restart","supersedes":"1e60b9dd6740e8fa3af86895562b252ab0729fca6883ae81e18e815e7a0c9eb7","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:12.781746Z","id":"1548bf8b9ff1b2344d7aa757f4defe4c21a2bc4f65282eb62140ade1511e8b29","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md section 7 has the WebView reload once a restarted daemon is up, so _AppPage reloads the surface when the endpoint's PID changes. The shell's own event stream reconnects by itself on the same port, so the reload only matters when the page's state went stale; it also discards a composer the person was typing into, and the page's scroll position unless the shell restores it. Reloading only when the shell does not report ready again within a short while would keep the draft.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3237},"end":{"line":3252},"content_hash":"0ffa89fd74813ff96f7b6365f3176f9106bc12904a3df70feddd7d4c8df59e2b"},"summary":"A daemon restart on the same port reloads the open app, dropping an unsent composer draft","supersedes":"16065304e8eab625b90a381011139ac6d8cef828f150ec11c0d1f44b6423a497","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:12.843560Z","id":"c09c59f7bd7daf4a3ccb4b534d80152b205b7b7b806607da5b768ebc586cd86c","body":{"detail":"_made holds one app and Timings.start(sayUsable) is started by each make (_make), so a second Make restarts the clock and the first app's ready no longer stops it. The defended number is only right for one make at a time.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":867},"end":{"line":868},"content_hash":"a0e043f9428c26b727c270a80fcf4bb6d712869347b09d2a22becb698a8676c7"},"summary":"say-usable is one slot: with several makes at once it measures from the latest Make to whichever app that run made","supersedes":"bb075ca4ceab5ecc1ee2d797aee15f3b5591da4e74675963a9dc6f0796b9342b","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:12.898782Z","id":"c7b6e945c95c659ed80755894a0d42f0232ef08522a5f255d54aaa94df190b99","body":{"detail":"The platform side (android/.../BackgroundRunService.kt Notices.news) treats the field as an opaque string extra and keys the notification ID by its hash, so it works without platform changes; but the convention lives only in app.dart. A typed BackgroundWork.question(title, text, qid) with its own tap stream would make it explicit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2104},"end":{"line":2104},"content_hash":"5cc6648706a4d640a900240ac3dfe82f3e35d3e215600e338488790bbbb9590e"},"summary":"A question notification rides on BackgroundWork.ready with the target 'question:<qid>' in its artifact field, which _onNews splits again","supersedes":"7f28c8ffe91ef10b071c668d3d70c9b37fdf38b4c21bc3d298cceddad56d3ae3","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:12.966861Z","id":"7a81b228bb180061b844c798a47b5e25e754550273e4126bcb2238aec2e3751f","body":{"detail":"ClaxPointerScope (lib/ui/kit/verbs.dart) records the kind from a translucent Listener at the root. Widget tests drive Flutter-drawn surfaces only. On Android the platform view's touches pass through Flutter's hit testing, so this likely holds there; on macOS it falls back to Click by platform before any event either way. The home app's chrome().pointer and the notifications' Tap/Click follow the same value.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3042},"end":{"line":3042},"content_hash":"ea118f4fd4593c995968e58cde5b18ee551960264645958f19ea01ce61eab3d4"},"suggested_fix":"Check on a Chromebook or Android with a mouse: move the mouse over the home app's page only, then trigger a no_gesture notice and read Tap or Click.","summary":"Whether pointer events over an app's WebView (a platform view) reach ClaxPointerScope's Listener is not verified on a device; if they do not, a Chromebook mouse used only in a page keeps saying Tap","supersedes":"c42ff35b4bbbf23e9d14576bd86690421ab97e3441fdbf2f99da8ef405b8d816","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.021094Z","id":"cbb3159b99672e45f4fd63052056b04d22199eaf8fabf3781557dddb7602ffa2","body":{"detail":"_mayRun answers false when _nav has no mounted context, and _gateRun then calls FeedbackWorker.cancelChange or stopBuild, so the comments stay stopped until a newer comment or Retry. Unlike DialogReadConsent (waiting: _runs.needsOk), the sheet posts no notification when Clax is in the background, so a change recovered at a launch that ends before the first frame would be stopped silently. Only the loop's gate is tested (test/agent/ai_consent_test.dart); no app-level test drives a change through _gateRun.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":882},"end":{"line":900},"content_hash":"7621ab8aec014d2d9b5516a210849ba555f2e7697893e60cb984cfc08cd093bd"},"summary":"A change or build the AI consent stops while no navigator is up is stopped as Stop stops it, with nothing told in the background","supersedes":"f749c22d8f0f376be905aa8188ca087c807146338a2fa3ae18600710a3b7a7a5","tags":["ios","untested","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.101835Z","id":"dfd222b76f435e0e47617977fdfd29c94be4abd82cce732abd0b8d4cb5a6d84b","body":{"detail":"PendingMake keeps only requests, so a stopped MakeSession does not come back after a quit; _offerLostMake then removes every 'new:' entry of unfinished.json. Up to $6 of drafted work is lost if Clax quits before Keep going. Keeping it would mean saving the stopped make's key with its request in PendingMake and offering it as a stopped tile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1841},"end":{"line":1855},"content_hash":"66ed153bd77c2b62fbd32bfc6448afe90f34af15e4db187538806cd496e1fdec"},"summary":"A make stopped at a limit is not kept across launches: its draft is forgotten at the next launch","supersedes":"83ac0c7bbb8659b8e6f6798fdf9f45654b647988b0eac46ca6541285e5ae3ef9","tags":["make","keep-going","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.155692Z","id":"8d79ea61f63325a966d272d5d9b0d58cdef63e7a8a22296b598d6164091490c7","body":{"detail":"Spec §5.11's Mac case opens the window with the sidebar drawn from HomeHost's cached lists and the working ClaxMark in the detail after 600 ms. _home returns ClaxSplash (or the launch snapshot) until the daemon's first Up creates HomeHost, and SidebarModel needs a HomeHost; nothing caches the lists across launches.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2808},"end":{"line":2812},"content_hash":"860feff50060936360dda048cb4b81efdc861d086d0e030a29cec554b652ffb0"},"summary":"The split window shows only once HomeHost exists: before the daemon is up the splash fills the window","supersedes":"ef5e2ac6e0936a00acbf5c8a18401dab8b9d274cd3bd08044cb2107ce899c8cb","tags":["macos","split","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.210258Z","id":"cddf83871b9bb1731927c3b1f78077edd1e610f7542545209d4755e9bedf4f9d","body":{"detail":"MakingScreen in the detail draws its leading (build-back, a chevron) through ClaxScaffold's Mac header in the toolbar row of the detail (WindowTitlebar.of), where macos/Runner/Toolbar.swift puts Back and Forward past the sidebar's edge. test/ui/shots/split_shots_test.dart draws the toolbar's items as stand-ins over it, so the render (split-make-mac-*.png) cannot show an overlap. The WKWebView preview at the pane's width (up to 960) is also seen only through a fake PreviewView.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2925},"end":{"line":2963},"content_hash":"4065c8f7d7eb77768568edf560df001acd0079f450fbe2af996adf20e897f0b4"},"summary":"The build view in a split window's detail is unverified in the running Mac app, and its Back header shares the toolbar row with the native Back and Forward","supersedes":"399cb81f8b4588605d9a72403d7f6ab0d486c1a4df40401c63daa601af07a86c","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:13.271806Z","id":"27ca66ca5354ffaed2c691678a5eb68d0dc76f9d177af028e61fc40d222b02a8","body":{"detail":"MakeService removes a made session from its list, so the make's row goes; SidebarModel.keeps (lib/ui/split/sidebar_model.dart:281) keeps MakeSelected while _paneMake names it, so MakingScreen can follow the build until Open app. No app test drives a make with a plan that goes on (the app_test rig hands the app over at once), and the window's title stays the request. _paneMake is cleared only when the view exits, not when the person selects something else.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2925},"end":{"line":2963},"content_hash":"4065c8f7d7eb77768568edf560df001acd0079f450fbe2af996adf20e897f0b4"},"summary":"A made make whose build goes on keeps its build view selected in the detail with no sidebar row selected; the path has no test","supersedes":"191a38cc31b740c096bf4df079981bcb6fec43a4abab9a348de51b80b740e3e9","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.771624Z","id":"fd74280cc86dc6a7a9f17f763f8436954ad8ec2321c49867d25f36fb6f0895b2","body":{"detail":"_failedAway and _offerLostMake push the build view from AppRoot (_makingRoute) and do not read its MakingResult. Edit there cancels the make (MakeSession.cancel) and pops EditRequest, which only the launcher's _showMake (lib/ui/launcher.dart) turns into a New sheet holding the request. Opened from the failed tile instead, Edit works.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1881},"end":{"line":1902},"content_hash":"416e057835a2775fa15f05dc69ef2cf2394ca18f8f4ceee4a0bd72c0359579c4"},"summary":"A build view opened from the failure toast or from Make it again ignores Edit: the request is dropped instead of reopening the New sheet","supersedes":"0a2664b07c2795e61f202eed5501b7681ea10c839da055901930003cacd92cc0","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.826685Z","id":"c7f7d2dbda3ec4768467e7f72d509b5f3c5f9094ec20d09d4c85642c45889d72","body":{"detail":"test/app_background_test.dart's tapped-notification test opens the asked question before the recheck queues the other, so the sheet it replaces is never showing; no test in test/app_test.dart or test/app_background_test.dart reaches removeRoute. By reading, the path is sound on the installed SDK: NavigatorState.removeRoute completes the route's future (navigator.dart:5733-5751, entry.complete), so whenComplete clears _sheetQuestion/_sheetRoute and shows the asked one, and a second asked question in the same window is queued without a second removeRoute (route.isActive is false). A regression here would leave a stuck _sheetQuestion and no further sheets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2268},"end":{"line":2280},"content_hash":"42da1536fe86615d7879ca3df7bb4cd3d6641b16ee94cfd750563cb9ae187a8e"},"suggested_fix":"A test in test/app_test.dart: a question about no app shows its sheet unasked, then the inbox opens a second; expect the second loaded, and after Close the first again.","summary":"The path where an asked question takes the place of an unasked sheet (removeRoute, then the old completion shows the asked one) has no test","supersedes":"cd7c2dac4b3dd02b0513fb7a6a30c0adf260f63ef4ac12c9945594f3ececdd5b","tags":["review","N2c","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.897803Z","id":"146ea0a22bab9c494a05f2f421c3ea527820c5ead614dd643d29859c04198a11","body":{"detail":"test/app_bundles_test.dart covers a file opened before the daemon is up, a refusal and forgetDeleted. Nothing tests that _recoverBundles shows one BundleNoticeSheet per RecoveredUpdate and the 'Shared apps' damaged notice exactly once (only _bundlesStarted guards them), that two files opened together show their sheets one after another through _bundleQueue, or that delete is false off Android (line 796): flutter test runs as android, so the macOS branch that must never delete the person's own file has no test. A sheet dropped because _nav.currentContext is null (line 763) also leaves Android's cache copy undeleted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1227},"end":{"line":1256},"content_hash":"5b8296a60c902f76d24abfd3e0a5251d060d942b187f674dc332cb4d66e4f041"},"suggested_fix":"App tests with debugDefaultTargetPlatformOverride = TargetPlatform.macOS asserting the opened file still exists; a pre-written snapshot under supportDir/snapshots and an unreadable lineage file, asserting each notice once across a daemon restart; two FakeBundleIntake.open calls in a row.","summary":"The start-up bundle wiring's notices and platform rule are untested: recoverInterrupted's notices, the damaged-lineage notice, several queued files, and macOS keeping the opened file","supersedes":"c8e36cbdd1773918755742af1ce5885ee80428176554a939988c804eef387a7d","tags":["bundles","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:14.969798Z","id":"ef30f28807809a49e2f06f28baefd13037ae32e626f2792c978ce221d4d561f1","body":{"detail":"In the app, both the home app and the built-in Launcher act through _homeFlows with contextOf: () => _nav.currentContext (the Navigator's own element). apps/clax_app/test/ui/launcher_test.dart builds Launcher without host, so its flows use the Launcher's context; apps/clax_app/test/home/home_route_test.dart checks the menu rect reaching HomeActions but not the flows. A context lookup that needs something below the Navigator (Overlay.of, Scaffold.of, a render box for a share origin in BundleFlows) would fail only in the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":802},"end":{"line":823},"content_hash":"d83c88c212d7019e11e0340f795fd95044cd253f3f6d6adcf1eb4f7497487878"},"suggested_fix":"Add an AppRoot-level widget test: a home device call openInbox/menu/newApp from the home AppScreen shows the inbox route, the menu sheet and the New app sheet, and the built-in Launcher with host: does the same.","summary":"No test drives HomeFlows over the app navigator's context: the home app's inbox, menu sheet, import and New app flows are tested only through a Launcher that builds its own HomeFlows","supersedes":"cea3964d1be5a9a92d0d968231bf8c129f5d0cd0f5c4a70647fff12685ac2166","tags":["review","home","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.026689Z","id":"80f222b5acec5bc870c453de44cb9d7d072f6b57100feaac7adf02ac04f3b29f","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/test/home/home_update_test.dart covers updateHomeApp over the real Updater and a FakeInspector; the wiring in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart that builds the Installer, passes updater.update and completes the sheet's Completer from _bundleQueue is exercised only on a device.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1264},"end":{"line":1315},"content_hash":"17aa31d34ea55c6fae1ed57dc276f075f72391287e4e9d62bdb1938674718bfb"},"summary":"The startup home update (updateHomeApp in _installHome) has no app-level test: no test passes shippedHome to AppRoot, so the ask callback over _bundleSheet, its null answer when no screen is up, and a null _updater (no inspector) are untested","supersedes":"4bab0857e48d0cbf80d12c9a12528cb65f7590d43225054745a679e9b96ed55a","tags":["home-app","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:00:15.093372Z","id":"8926f058fdf5f3fcbdc61f0a20781950b153866034072c23c35128d0c6216e73","body":{"detail":"The home app's WebView is made by the home route at the daemon's first Up, so its process start, the shell's load and the page's first render follow the daemon's start. On the macOS release build main to the home app's first shown took 358-632 ms over five cold starts (f1c07f346b12), small enough that a WebView made before Up, handed its base URL later, was not worth a new AppSurface factory.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2726},"end":{"line":2747},"content_hash":"724e9d016bca5ed683d5fb6fb6d5cb258d45dfe56be04c76919e86bb126a7e56"},"summary":"Start the home app's WebView (WebKit's or Chromium's process) before the daemon is up, and load the shell once it is","supersedes":"21417a8a8d4ccfaed3198e447cbccbd70efccbab9c06cc73a995dcbe798eac4c","tags":["time-to-usable","revisit:home-usable on the phone is over the target set from its first measurement","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:03.809719Z","id":"803fa7e215b9fe4035f200caa893c453ec50e9e717c21fa06b47ad26af493f3a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: an app opened at a thread, a version or a comment, or with an action, shows in the split window's detail and is one of _openApps (AppRootState._openInPane, _paneApp); 'a split window opens an app aimed somewhere beside its sidebar' (wide Android, the Mac, and a notice's later action reaching the same screen) in test/app_test.dart passes (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:app_test)","supersedes":"4050e41739e610b48071a5d4e89041c50a3b71ebe19a818fe9ef1b87cc9667ea","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T23:01:36.129232Z","id":"38fbc088d5b9244065254f9645150f914b1be140a867b10dbb697ad005b7753d","body":{"detail":"A pushed app route behaves alike (each aimed open pushes a new page). Aiming the existing page (OpenThread, LoadVersion on its surface) would keep it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2868},"end":{"line":2872},"content_hash":"d565b69ebf6c472750d6fb57b77f236902e546b56ca28e4c4bf35119c69d54d1"},"summary":"Opening the app already in a split window's detail at a thread, a version or a comment builds its screen again (a new _paneAim generation), reloading the page and dropping an unsent composer draft","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:11:43.878030Z","id":"369d1db8a209a4f1d4c7a7f32ff5fda11b92c6127a9208e32d7d8b9f35429921","body":{"detail":"_onState runs its open branch (HomeHost, the stream, the worker) on the first CoreOpening, so calls wait in the core while it backs up and migrates (CoreOpening 'backing up' / 'migrating' with done/total, lib/core/core_client.dart). A large old home's migration then shows the built-in launcher or the home snapshot with nothing loading, instead of the splash; the phases CoreHost.state carries are not shown anywhere.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1484},"end":{"line":1556},"content_hash":"5afbf00c960048cb90e10e9baf3cbef3fd9abfd1e296e592b19aabc677493e7f"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the splash while CoreHost.state is CoreOpening with phase 'backing up' or 'migrating' (and show done/total), opening the launcher at the first other state; the home snapshot can still cover.","summary":"The app treats an opening core as open: the launcher shows at once and a long migration runs behind it with no splash or progress","tags":["core","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:11:43.880743Z","id":"c20f5c812d35fd5170281697e6ce66bde693951687b5f89747672f7cbbbc3d0e","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design section 2.6 has Android's onTrimMemory call POST /api/core/trim as iOS does. IosBackgroundWork takes onTrim (lib/platform/background_work.dart); ChannelBackgroundWork and MainActivity have no trim message.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":154},"content_hash":"d4b0da3d2c2a3f3a23ce9d824d0d0aae5cc52a1e1b34e58e44cef605becc5f11"},"suggested_fix":"Post 'trim' on dev.empathic.clax/background from MainActivity.onTrimMemory and answer it in ChannelBackgroundWork with CoreHost.trim.","summary":"Android's onTrimMemory does not reach CoreHost.trim; only iOS's background channel calls it","tags":["core","android","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T23:06:43.770389Z","id":"a9b4f3435b67ab284adb18848a586e42f6cbb7c32ddb5edabea3d2739d056b08","body":{"detail":"Fixed in f1c07f346b12. `bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:platform_background_work_test` PASSED, with 'trim from Android is answered once the core trimmed; a failed trim is answered too' (test/platform/background_work_test.dart). On the Android emulator (android-36 arm64, //apps/clax_app:apk at f1c07f346b12), `adb shell am send-trim-memory dev.empathic.clax RUNNING_LOW` reached the running app without a crash (its PID unchanged); the core itself was not open there (see the clax-embed core.lock blocker).","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"ClaxApplication.onTrimMemory sends 'trim' on dev.empathic.clax/background, and ChannelBackgroundWork(onTrim: core.trim) answers it once CoreHost.trim completes","supersedes":"c20f5c812d35fd5170281697e6ce66bde693951687b5f89747672f7cbbbc3d0e","tags":["reason:fixed","android","core","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T23:52:58.918007Z","id":"66a3e807e1686fc950a1cd094e3f9a99769b995d131d344e961e427af8c52b12","body":{"detail":"importJsonState (apps/clax_app/lib/core/json_import.dart) and its runner hook (EffectRunner.importState, run before each LoadJobs) are built and tested, but main.dart starts the queue without importJson. In the UI isolate the feedback worker still runs every change (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart AgentRuntime's FeedbackWorker; the worker isolate's queue runs makes only, app.dart 'Changes are the feedback worker's unless the queue given shows them') and keeps change-ledger.json, asked.json, stopped.json and unfinished.json (lib/agent/worker.dart, lib/agent/loop.dart, lib/agent/tools/finish.dart), plans.json (PlanStore: the build view and the feedback worker's builds) and agent-read-consent.json (FileConsentMemory: DialogReadConsent, AgentReadPermissions). With the import on: (1) every launch would delete those live files after the import answers already, so the feedback worker would lose its stops, ledger, asked questions and unfinished drafts across restarts; (2) the first launch would make queued change jobs from the ledger and asked entries that the worker isolate runs while the feedback worker recovers the same threads from the core, so a change could run or reply twice. The import key app-json-v1 is one-shot, so importing only the retired file (pending-make.json) now would leave the other six never imported. Options: (a) turn it on once changes run on the worker isolate's queue and the UI isolate's file stores are gone; (b) turn it on now and accept (1) and (2); (c) import without deleting the six live files and mark the import done on the Dart side, accepting that what the feedback worker writes afterwards is never imported.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":182},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"1a37ca407c36d73bcea12e7da70c74c2b2682caa2a10be121548fbe5b8d3ae00"},"suggested_fix":"Option (a): pass importJson: true in main.dart's startQueue in the change that moves changes to the worker isolate and deletes the file stores.","summary":"The app does not run the one-time JSON import yet (QueueHost.start without importJson): when may it be turned on?","tags":["task:29","task:30","import","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T23:52:58.918490Z","id":"3e456fd9597abedeb1c26eb3bc8b98af8a1c13923317fbf1a8d40e72f666da35","body":{"detail":"Task 30b (delete pending_make, ledger, stops and the file stores of unfinished, asked and plan) deleted nothing, because none of them is dead: FileChangeLedger and FileAskedQuestions are the feedback worker's (lib/agent/loop.dart, lib/agent/tools/finish.dart, lib/agent/worker.dart; also integration_test/rig.dart:190 and ios_rig.dart:274); FileStoppedThreads is AgentRuntime's (lib/app.dart:996); FileUnfinishedChanges is the app's (lib/app.dart:1186) for changes stopped at a limit and the stopped makes' drafts; PlanStore(file:) feeds BuildLink, the build view and the feedback worker's builds (lib/app.dart:1185, tool/eval/live_build.dart:121); PendingMake is the local queue's (lib/ui/local_queue.dart via LocalMakes, the debug scripted-agent and test path where no worker isolate runs); FileConsentMemory is DialogReadConsent's. They can go once changes, builds and read consents run on the core's jobs (record on lib/main.dart:182-200).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":234},"end":{"line":272},"content_hash":"8d28071ae0bfc0e922790b8958c03c12e98d1bdf613d9f9fe385bf545f630a44"},"summary":"The JSON state stores the import replaces stay: each still has a live caller in the UI isolate","tags":["task:30","import","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:16:59.347853Z","id":"a349fad914779c9c33482997cdd5f1c675b12b37acb59110333f345c8de57468","body":{"detail":"With the worker's queue (_localQueue null), _offerLostMake returns before PendingMake.takeEach, leaving pending-make.json for the JSON import, which apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart:185-200 does not turn on (QueueHost.start without importJson, record 66a3e807). So a make an earlier app had in flight when it ended is neither shown as an interrupted tile nor run: the person does not learn it was lost until the import runs. Options: (a) show each make, read-only from the file, with a 'Make it again' offer through the existing make flow; the import must then leave out a make already made again (for example by giving the made-again job the ID the import would mint, crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs job_id) or it runs twice, and the offer must not repeat at every launch; this is a UI feature whose design questions are open; (b) turn the import on (record 66a3e807), which imports each as a queued make; (c) leave it as is until (b).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2075},"end":{"line":2081},"content_hash":"880eb8878d99a4a436c92a9729d5f51238052c8e9e5d4b7850a43f4f189ac14c"},"summary":"An old app's interrupted make (pending-make.json) is neither shown nor run while the JSON import is off","tags":["status:needs-decision","queue","import","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:16:59.350357Z","id":"4d137c74225a084aba37ae3fe89f1dd23723d710c21129b931f951d6059fd525","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"66a3e807e1686fc950a1cd094e3f9a99769b995d131d344e961e427af8c52b12","summary":"Two latent defects behind this switch are fixed: a landed, unreplied ledger change now imports with a turn:1 finish call before its publish step, so the queue posts the reply instead of failing it invalid_step (f1c07f346b12); an unfinished change's carry is imported in the worker's shape and Keep going seeds the carried draft (f1c07f346b12). apps/clax_app/test/core/json_import_real_test.dart runs both against the real core. Still open before the switch: the concern on crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs's ledger (a landed version's documents never written) and the needs-decision concern on apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart's _offerLostMake (pending-make.json).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T19:03:54.597882Z","id":"9e30ddf44d21f8d53b12947d83b569a7676b118ffa15045be37529ebc3523f5a","body":{"detail":"ClaxSplash (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/splash.dart) continues Android's system splash at the same size and place, so it was left as it is; once the core is up the home app's page shows under AppScreen's AppCover with CoverTiming (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_cover.dart). The hand-off from the 132-wide splash mark to the 28-wide cover mark is a change of size on screen. Whether the splash should follow the same timing, or the cover reuse the splash's mark, is open.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2875},"end":{"line":2877},"content_hash":"bd61b4ff1db9a5d09fedf3f57eb5c4b586f7e8b20952fccf4bdcebbf3b8589cd"},"summary":"Before the core is up a cold start shows ClaxSplash (the mark at rest from the first frame, breathing after 600 ms), not the loading cover's 100 ms plain surface and held breath","tags":["ui","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T20:03:16.393674Z","id":"761ceba728b1b984d1cc4b0ab3772257211206f06645e007e4f3a330f884f674","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3265},"end":{"line":3315},"content_hash":"db30d272c39934ca9a8ccd1a994639c9283de3c73a8c59309308475996817371"},"summary":"No app-level test drives an update through _appScreen: _UpdateGate's one title lookup (_titleOf) and the cover over AppScreen are tested only through UpdatingCover alone (test/ui/updating_cover_test.dart)","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T21:56:42.654723Z","id":"dab24784cf7a951a85eb1b40bd281cb5918c4d8ef6158a2baa8c696131390d1e","body":{"kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3273},"end":{"line":3323},"content_hash":"db30d272c39934ca9a8ccd1a994639c9283de3c73a8c59309308475996817371"},"summary":"No app-level test drives an update through _appScreen: _UpdateGate's one title lookup (_titleOf) and the cover over AppScreen are tested only through UpdatingCover alone (test/ui/updating_cover_test.dart)","supersedes":"761ceba728b1b984d1cc4b0ab3772257211206f06645e007e4f3a330f884f674","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
